{
	id: basics-02-items-damage
	version: 1
	kind: tutorial
	title: The Basics: Items and Damage
	author: asdf
	format: scenario
	human: freeps
	opponent: {
		name: Items Tutorial
		fallback: pass
	}
	coverage: strict
	options: {
		autoPass: maneuver, archery, assignment, regroup
	}
	cards: {
		freeps: {
			# Frodo, Resolute Hobbit
			frodo: 10_121
			# The One Ring, The Ruling Ring
			ring: 1_2
			# Aragorn, Heir of Elendil
			aragorn: 4_109
			# Ranger's Sword
			rangersword: 1_112
			# Gondorian Blade
			blade: 11_59
			# Great Shield
			shield: 1_107
			# Athelas
			athelas: 1_94
			# Narya
			narya: 3_34
			# Hobbit Sword
			hobbitsword: 1_299
			# Athelas
			athelas2: 1_94
			# Old Toby
			old: 1_305
			# Gandalf, The Grey Pilgrim
			gandalf: 2_122
			# Glamdring
			glamdring: 1_75
			# Armor
			armor: 1_92
			# Gimli's Battle Axe
			battleaxe: 1_14
			# Gimli's Helm
			helm: 1_15
			# Coat of Mail
			mail: 1_101
		}
		shadow: {
			# Frodo, Resolute Hobbit
			oppFrodo: 10_121
			# The One Ring, The Ruling Ring
			oppRing: 1_2
			# Uruk-hai Raiding Party
			raidingparty: 1_158
			# Orthanc Berserker
			berserker: 3_66
			# Orthanc Warrior
			warrior1: 4_165
			# Orthanc Warrior
			warrior2: 4_165
			# Bred for Battle
			bred: 1_121
			# Lurtz's Sword
			lurtzs: 2_43
		}
	}
	ringBearer: {
		freeps: frodo
		shadow: oppFrodo
	}
	ring: {
		freeps: ring
		shadow: oppRing
	}
	# Green Hill Country, Trollshaw Forest, Rivendell Valley, Pass of Caradhras, The Bridge of Khazad-dûm, Dimrill Dale, Silverlode Banks, Pillars of the Kings, Summit of Amon Hen
	sites: {
		freeps: 1_323, 1_334, 1_341, 1_348, 1_349, 1_350, 1_355, 1_358, 1_362
		shadow: 1_323, 1_334, 1_341, 1_348, 1_349, 1_350, 1_355, 1_358, 1_362
	}
	rules: {
		oneSided: true
		freeps: [
			{
				type: modifier
				modifier: {
					type: modifyHandSize
					amount: -3
				}
			}
			{
				type: modifier
				modifier: {
					type: disableGameText
					filter: name(The One Ring)
				}
			}
			{
				type: modifier
				modifier: {
					type: skipPhase
					phase: maneuver
				}
			}
		]
		shadow: [
			{
				type: modifier
				modifier: {
					type: modifyRoamingPenalty
					filter: minion
					amount: -2
				}
			}
		]
	}
	setup: {
		freeps: {
			characters: aragorn
			hand: rangersword, blade, shield, athelas, hobbitsword, athelas2, old
			deck: narya
		}
		shadow: {
			hand: raidingparty, berserker
		}
	}
	outcome: {
		lose: {
			type: hasCardInDeadPile
			filter: companion
		}
		loseMessage: One of your companions has fallen, and the fellowship cannot go on without them. Go back to the last checkpoint and look at the numbers again: who is about to be overwhelmed, and which card in your hand can stop it?
	}
	steps: [
		# ---- 1
		{
			pause: true
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					header: The Basics, Part 2: Items and Damage
					text: "In the previous tutorial, your fellowship fought past the hordes of [Moria] Moria with nothing but their own power and the occasional burst of energy via Events.\n\nToday we will look at the importance of **Items**, which are **Possessions** and **Artifacts** your companions will wield to defend themselves and their friends."
				}
				{
					text: **Possessions** represent different weapons, cloaks, staves, shields, and other physical objects that people carry with them.
					zoom: card:rangersword
					focus: type
				}
				{
					text: "Most often these items will grant some sort of strength or vitality bonus to their bearer, but many also come with useful game text.  The right sword in the right hand can make all the difference.\n\nThe game text will also tell you who can hold the possession."
					zoom: card:rangersword
					focus: strength, text
				}
			]
		}
		# ---- 2
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Let's play the Ranger's Sword on Aragorn.
					anchor: card:rangersword
					highlight: card:rangersword
				}
			]
			allow: play(rangersword)
		}
		# ---- 3
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: As you can see, cards played on companions are placed underneath with the left edge sticking out.  This lets us see the stat bonuses and title of those cards without taking up so much space.
					anchor: card:rangersword
					highlight: card:rangersword
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: Gemp has automatically increased Aragorn's strength to show the sum of his parts: 8 base strength + 2 strength from the sword.  Remember, you can hover over Aragorn or right-click him to see the actual numbers on the card itself.
					anchor: card:aragorn:strength
					highlight: card:aragorn
					side: right
				}
				{
					text: The [[Ranger's Sword]] has an **Item Class** of "Hand Weapon".  Characters can only hold 1 kind of each item class at a time: they may only have 1 hand weapon, 1 cloak, 1 armor, and so on.
					anchor: card:rangersword
					highlight: card:rangersword
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: Since [[Gondorian Blade]] is also a **Hand Weapon**, Aragorn cannot wield it; he already has one sword and can't hold another.
					anchor: card:blade
					highlight: card:blade
					highlightStyle: red
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: However, he can hold a [[Great Shield]], since its item class is **Shield** and he does not have one of those.  Let's put that on him now.
					anchor: card:shield
					highlight: card:shield
				}
			]
			allow: play(shield)
		}
		# ---- 4
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "[[Athelas]] does not have an Item Class.  You can have as many such items as you want on your characters.   Play both copies of Athelas on him now."
					anchor: zone:self.hand
					highlight: card:athelas, card:athelas2
					highlightStyle: green
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: play(athelas)?, play(athelas2)?
			answer: play(athelas)
		}
		# ---- 5
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "[[Athelas]] does not have an Item Class.  You can have as many such items as you want on your characters.   Play both copies of Athelas on him now."
					anchor: zone:self.hand
					highlight: card:athelas, card:athelas2
					highlightStyle: green
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: play(athelas)?, play(athelas2)?
			answer: play(athelas2)
		}
		# ---- 6
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "All four of these Possessions were automatically played on Aragorn, because he is the only [Gondor] **Gondor** Companion on the table.\n\nWhen you only have 1 valid target for a card, Gemp will choose that target for you automatically."
					anchor: card:rangersword
					highlight: card:rangersword
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: Remember, the Ring-bearer is the most important companion on the field.  Let's play a [[Hobbit Sword]] on Frodo so he can defend himself.
					anchor: card:hobbitsword
					highlight: card:hobbitsword
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: play(hobbitsword)
		}
		# ---- 7
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: +2 strength may not seem like a lot, but Frodo can now only be overwhelmed by minions totalling strength 12 or more (instead of 8).  Even a little bit adds up.
					anchor: card:frodo
					highlight: card:frodo:strength
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: "[[Old Toby]] is a Possession that is not held by a companion.  Instead, it goes to the **Support Area**, a place where cards go to represent being available to the Fellowship without being in any one particular place.\n\nLet's play Old Toby."
					anchor: card:old
					highlight: card:old
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: play(old)
		}
		# ---- 8
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Old Toby is now in the **Support Area**, in a row beneath your companions.
					anchor: card:old
					highlight: card:old
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: Your opponent's **Support Area** is up here.  Keep an eye on cards that they play here; unlike Minions, Possessions and other cards in the Support Area are not discarded automatically when you reconcile.  They will continue to affect the world for many turns to come.
					anchor: zone:opp.support
					highlight: zone:opp.support
				}
				{
					text: Old Toby has game text that triggers when it plays to draw a card.  Since it is optional, you have to click on Old Toby to activate it, or else Pass.
					anchor: card:old
					highlight: card:old
				}
			]
			allow: use(old)?, pass?
			answer: use(old)
		}
		# ---- 9
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Now that we've played our items, let's move to the next site.
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
					side: right
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 10
		{
			when: shadow, action, phase(shadow), turn(1)
			answer: play(berserker)
		}
		# ---- 11
		{
			when: shadow, action, phase(shadow), turn(1)
			answer: play(raidingparty)
		}
		# ---- 12
		{
			pause: true
			when: freeps, assign, phase(assignment), turn(1)
			messages: [
				During the **Shadow Phase**, your opponent played a pair of Minions.
				{
					text: "We saw [Moria] **Moria** Orcs last time, but this time we see [Isengard] **Isengard** Uruk-hai.  \n\nThese uruks are savage and powerful, and almost all of them have the **Damage +1** keyword.  This means that at the end of a skirmish, if they win, they will apply 1 more wound than normal.  Those wounds will add up fast!"
					zoom: card:raidingparty
				}
				"With both minions at least strength 9, Frodo would have been in trouble without his sword.  \n\nAnd with both Uruks combining to 20 strength, Aragorn would be overwhelmed if he took on both at once, so it's a good thing that our Ring-bearer can defend himself!"
			]
		}
		# ---- 13 (skirmish1)
		{
			id: skirmish1
			checkpoint: true
			when: freeps, assign, phase(assignment), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Assign the Uruks to your companions and resolve their skirmishes.  Don't forget to click Done to lock in your assignment choice.
					anchor: card:berserker
					highlight: card:berserker
					side: above
				}
			]
			answer: assign(frodo: raidingparty, aragorn: berserker)
		}
		# ---- 14
		{
			when: freeps, cards, phase(assignment), turn(1)
			answer: choose(aragorn)
		}
		# ---- 15
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(skirmish), turn(1)
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 16
		{
			when: freeps, cards, phase(skirmish), turn(1)
			answer: choose(frodo)
		}
		# ---- 17
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(skirmish), turn(1)
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 18
		{
			when: freeps, choice, phase(regroup), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: That extra damage is stacking up!
					anchor: card:frodo:wounds
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: We had better stay and hide, reconciling our hand and getting rid of these ferocious Uruks.
					anchor: ui:dialog
				}
			]
			allow: option(No)
		}
		# ---- 19
		{
			when: freeps, cards, phase(regroup), turn(1)
			messages: [
				{
					text: We don't want to discard any of the cards we have now when reconciling, so let's just click Done.
					anchor: ui:button:done
					highlight: ui:button:done
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 20
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Oh good, we've found Gandalf!  Let's play him so you can also play some of his items.
					anchor: card:gandalf
					highlight: card:gandalf
				}
			]
			allow: play(gandalf)
		}
		# ---- 21
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "[[Glamdring]] is a Hand Weapon, granting Gandalf +2 strength and **Damage +1** of his own.  In addition, it has a very handy Fellowship special ability!  Let's play it now."
					anchor: card:glamdring
					highlight: card:glamdring
				}
			]
			allow: play(glamdring)
		}
		# ---- 22
		{
			pause: true
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: Site 2, [[Trollshaw Forest]], activated an automatic required trigger by playing a possession.  Because it's not optional (no "may"), we did not have to click on it to draw a card.
					anchor: ui:site:2
					highlight: ui:site:2
					side: right
				}
			]
		}
		# ---- 23
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "But back to Glamdring.\n\n**Special Abilities** are bold text actions that you can use in the matching phases, like Events.  Unlike Events, you do not discard the card afterwards, and so you can use the ability as many times as you can afford to do so."
					zoom: card:glamdring
				}
				{
					text: "[[Glamdring]]'s **Fellowship** ability has two parts: its **Costs** and **Effects**, separated by the word \"to\". \n\nIn this case, if we use its ability, we have to exert Gandalf as a cost.  The effect will be revealing our opponent's hand, and removing twilight from the **Twilight Pool**."
					zoom: card:glamdring
					focus: text
				}
				{
					text: "Remember, \"exert\" means to put a non-lethal wound on a character.\n\nClick on Glamdring to use its ability."
					anchor: card:glamdring
					highlight: card:glamdring
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: use(glamdring)
		}
		# ---- 24
		{
			when: freeps, arbitrary, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Here is your opponent's hand. The contents of the revealed cards will also show up in the **Combat Log** if you need to refer to them later.\n\nClick Done to dismiss the window."
					anchor: ui:dialog
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 25
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Glamdring's special ability could be used again if you wanted to, but in this case it wouldn't do you any good since you've already seen what's in your opponent's hand.\n\n(The twilight removal might matter on a repeat in some cases, but your opponent had no Orcs this time.)\n\nIn general, bold text special abilities can be used as many times as you can afford it."
					anchor: card:glamdring
					highlight: card:glamdring
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: One of the cards you drew was Narya; let's look closer at that.
					anchor: card:narya
					highlight: card:narya
				}
				{
					text: "[[Narya]] is an **Artifact**, not a Possession.  In practice, these two card types behave almost the same; the only important distinction is that if a card targets a Possession, it cannot target an Artifact, or vice versa.\n\nArtifacts tend to be more powerful than Possessions; +1 **Vitality** is a strong basic effect, even without the card text.\n\nHaving more vitality is one way to combat additional damage bonuses!"
					zoom: card:narya
				}
				{
					text: Play [[Narya]] on Gandalf.
					anchor: card:narya
					highlight: card:narya
				}
			]
			allow: play(narya)
		}
		# ---- 26
		{
			note: You've also drawn [[Armor]].  Let's play that on Aragorn.
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: You also drew [[Armor]].
					anchor: card:armor
					highlight: card:armor
					side: above
				}
				{
					text: "[[Armor]] protects the bearer from taking more than one wound in a skirmish.  This makes it ideal for shrugging off the extra hits from **Damage +1** Uruk-hai."
					zoom: card:armor
				}
				{
					text: Play [[Armor]] on Aragorn.
					anchor: card:armor
					highlight: card:armor
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: play(armor)
		}
		# ---- 27
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: The [[Athelas]] that you played earlier also has a special ability: when used, you can discard Athelas to heal a companion.  Let's use both of these to heal up your companions.
					anchor: card:shield
					highlight: card:athelas
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: use(athelas)?, use(athelas2)?
			answer: use(athelas)
		}
		# ---- 28
		{
			when: freeps, cards, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			skipWhen: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: The [[Athelas]] that you played earlier also has a special ability: when used, you can discard Athelas to heal a companion.  Let's use both of these to heal up your companions.
					anchor: card:armor
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: choose(gandalf)?, choose(frodo)?, choose(aragorn)?
			answer: choose(frodo)
		}
		# ---- 29
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: "Athelas requires you to discard itself, so we can't really use its ability more than once.\n\nHowever, you can use the second copy.  Use that to heal up your companions."
					anchor: card:shield
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: use(athelas)?, use(athelas2)?
			answer: use(athelas2)
		}
		# ---- 30
		{
			when: freeps, cards, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			skipWhen: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: The [[Athelas]] that you played earlier also has a special ability: when used, you can discard Athelas to heal a companion.  Let's use these to heal up Gandalf and Frodo.
					anchor: card:shield
					side: above
				}
			]
			allow: choose(gandalf)?, choose(frodo)?, choose(aragorn)?
			answer: choose(gandalf)
		}
		# ---- 31
		{
			when: freeps, action, phase(fellowship), turn(2)
			messages: [
				{
					text: We've played all the items we can manage for now.  Click Pass to end the **Fellowship Phase** and move on to the next site.
					anchor: ui:button:pass
					highlight: ui:button:pass
					side: right
				}
			]
			allow: pass
		}
		# ---- 32
		{
			when: shadow, action, phase(shadow), turn(2)
			answer: play(warrior1)
		}
		# ---- 33
		{
			when: shadow, action, phase(shadow), turn(2)
			answer: play(warrior2)
		}
		# ---- 34: these in whatever order the game asks for them
		{
			note: Turn 2. The assignment and both skirmishes, in whatever order the player takes them.
			when: turn(2)
			until: phase(regroup)
			anyOrder: [
				# -- 34.1
				{
					once: true
					when: freeps, assign
					messages: [
						"Your opponent played 2 Uruk-hai during their **Shadow Phase**.\n\nNow that we're in the **Assignment Phase**, assign the Warriors to Aragorn and Gandalf.  There's no need to have Frodo skirmish this time since you have ample protectors.\n\nClick Done once you're ready to lock in your assignments."
					]
					allow: {
						answers: assign(aragorn: warrior1, gandalf: warrior2)?, assign(aragorn: warrior2, gandalf: warrior1)?
						otherwise: Frodo would lose a skirmish, and there's no need to take those extra wounds given that Gandalf and Aragorn are both strong enough to win their respective skirmishes.
					}
					answer: assign(aragorn: warrior1, gandalf: warrior2)
				}
				# -- 34.2
				{
					when: freeps, cards, text(next skirmish)
					answer: choose(gandalf), choose(aragorn)
				}
				# -- 34.3
				{
					once: true
					when: freeps, action, fighting(aragorn)
					allow: pass
				}
				# -- 34.4
				{
					once: true
					when: opponent, action, fighting(aragorn)
					messages: [
						Here come the drums.
					]
					answer: play(bred)
				}
				# -- 34.5
				{
					when: opponent, cards, fighting(warrior1)
					answer: choose(warrior1)
				}
				# -- 34.6
				{
					when: opponent, cards
					answer: choose(warrior2)
				}
				# -- 34.7
				{
					when: freeps, action, phase(skirmish)
					answer: pass
				}
			]
		}
	]
}
